  "summary": "At an August 2026 Marietta, Oklahoma City Council meeting to decide on adopting Flock Safety license plate readers after a trial, Police Chief Brett Harris halted the partnership mid-meeting after a Flock representative disclosed that camera data is retained indefinitely rather than for the 30 days the department had agreed to. The council then unanimously voted the measure down.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "Folks, we're not moving forward any further. Marietta Police Department, Marietta city limits won't have Flock cameras",
      "paragraph_idx": 11
    },
    {
      "quote": "They're retaining data indefinitely, and that's exactly what our spectators complained about\u2014that the data doesn't disappear like they say it does",
      "paragraph_idx": 13
    },
    {
      "quote": "This system is not for Marietta, Oklahoma",
      "paragraph_idx": 18
    }
